Article 4: Where a foreign national establishes an employment relationship with an employer within the territory of the People's Republic of China, and under any of the following circumstances, the foreign national requests confirmation of the existence of a labor relationship with the employer, the People's Court shall support such request according to law:
(1) The foreign national has obtained permanent residence status;
(2) The foreign national has obtained a work permit and lawfully stays or resides within the territory of China;
(3) The foreign national has gone through the relevant procedures in accordance with the relevant provisions of the State.

Article 7: Where a worker requests the employer to pay double wages on the ground that the employer has not concluded a written labor contract, the People's Court shall support such request according to law, unless the employer adduces evidence to prove the existence of any of the following circumstances:
(1) The failure to conclude the contract is due to force majeure;
(2) The failure to conclude the contract is due to the worker's own intentional act or gross negligence;
(3) Other circumstances prescribed by laws or administrative regulations.

Article 8: Where a labor contract expires and any of the following circumstances exists, the People's Court shall determine that the term of the labor contract is automatically extended according to law, and such extension shall not be deemed as a situation where the employer has not concluded a written labor contract:
(1) The circumstances under Article 42 of the Labor Contract Law where the employer may not dissolve the labor contract;
(2) The service period specified in Article 17 of the Regulations on the Implementation of the Labor Contract Law has not yet expired;
(3) The term of office specified in Article 19 of the Trade Union Law has not expired.

Article 10: Where any of the following circumstances exists, the People's Court shall determine that the condition of "having concluded a fixed-term labor contract twice consecutively" under Article 14, paragraph 2, subparagraph (3) of the Labor Contract Law is satisfied:
(1) The employer and the worker have negotiated to extend the term of the labor contract and the cumulative extension reaches one year or more, and the extension period has expired;
(2) The employer and the worker have agreed that the labor contract shall be automatically renewed upon expiration, and the renewal period has expired;
(3) The worker continues to work at the original workplace and position for reasons not attributable to the worker, the employer changes the subject of the labor contract, but continues to exercise labor management over the worker, and the contract term expires;
(4) A labor contract is concluded again through other circumventing acts that violate the principle of good faith, and the term expires.

Article 16: After the employer illegally dissolves or terminates the labor contract, if any of the following circumstances exists, the People's Court may determine that the labor contract "cannot be further performed" as provided in Article 48 of the Labor Contract Law:
(1) The labor contract expires during arbitration or litigation, and there are no circumstances requiring renewal or extension of the labor contract according to law;
(2) The worker has begun to receive basic pension insurance benefits according to law;
(3) The employer is declared bankrupt;
(4) The employer is dissolved, except for dissolution due to merger or division;
(5) The worker has established a labor relationship with another employer, which seriously affects the completion of the original employer's work tasks, or fails to dissolve the labor relationship with the other employer after being requested by the original employer;
(6) Other circumstances exist where the labor contract objectively cannot be performed.

Article 17: Where the employer fails to organize a pre-departure occupational health examination for workers engaged in operations exposed to occupational disease hazards in accordance with the provisions of the safety production supervision and management department and the health administrative department of the State Council, and the worker requests to continue performing the labor contract after both parties have dissolved the labor contract, the People's Court shall support such request according to law, except under any of the following circumstances:
(1) Before the conclusion of the debate in the first instance trial, the employer has organized the worker to undergo an occupational health examination, and the examination results show that the worker does not suffer from an occupational disease;
(2) Before the conclusion of the debate in the first instance trial, the employer organizes the worker to undergo an occupational health examination, but the worker refuses to undergo the examination without justifiable reasons.
